{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"roleHeading":"Case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"coloredNeighbors","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.coloredNeighbors","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Coloring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/Coloring.swift#L144"},"symbolKind":"case","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO16coloredNeighborsyA2CmF"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IGRAPH_COLORING_GREEDY_COLORED_NEIGHBORS"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex_coloring_greedy(method= \"colored_neighbors\")"},{"type":"text","text":"): first the vertex of greatest degree (the least index on ties), then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeatedly the uncoloured vertex with the most coloured neighbours, ties as igraph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed binary heap breaks them (so not by index), which this follows step for step: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same colouring as igraph on simple graphs (igraph counts each parallel edge). O((n + m)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log n)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/coloredneighbors"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"colored